# PID tuning results as one dashboard. On top, the UR5e: pidtuna's four-rung ladder (factory → analytic → tuned →
# oracle) replayed on one coordinated tape, as KPI tiles, joint angles and errors over time, MuJoCo replays and the tool
# path, all on one clock. Below, all nine simulated robots, gains against the error they buy, and the one real
# comparison (the sim plant vs the rack).
# Data: source/build.py (round 1: pidtuna-website's exported JSON, sim and illustrative; sim_fidelity.json, real),
# source/build_replay.py (round 2: the UR5e and lever replays and MuJoCo renders, all sim) and source/build_headline.py
# (headline.json: kpis.json's cells copied beside each other for the tiles' deltas).
# Grammar: docs/peps/0004-dashboards.md; cards and the clock: docs/peps/0005-dashboard-cards.md.
data: gains.json
facets:
  - robot
  - { property: rung, order: [factory, analytic, tuned, oracle] }
  - { property: joint, searchable: true, limit: 6 }
properties:
  robot: { displayName: Robot }
  rung: { displayName: Rung }
  joint: { displayName: Joint }
  # declared rounding for the tables: Kp to 0.1, Kd to 0.01 (Kp runs 9.86 to 100,000); gains.json and joints.json keep every digit
  kp: { displayName: Kp, decimals: 1 }
  kd: { displayName: Kd, decimals: 2 }
  tracking_rms: { displayName: Tracking RMS }
  stop_p90: { displayName: Stop p90 }
  max_error: { displayName: Max error }
  ringing: { displayName: Ringing }
  improvement: { displayName: × better than factory }
  tuned_tracking_rms: { displayName: Tuned tracking RMS }
  oracle_tracking_rms: { displayName: Oracle }
  tuned_vs_oracle: { displayName: Tuned ÷ oracle }
  servo: { displayName: Servo }
  ff_fraction: { displayName: Coulomb feed-forward }
  situation: { displayName: Rung }
  q_deg: { displayName: Angle }
  q_target_deg: { displayName: Target angle }
  err_mrad: { displayName: Error }
  factory_stop_p90: { displayName: Factory }
  vs_factory: { displayName: × better than factory }
  stop_p90_mrad: { displayName: Stop p90 }
  tracking_rms_mrad: { displayName: Tracking RMS }
  max_error_mrad: { displayName: Max error }
  ringing_mrad: { displayName: Ringing }
  saturation: { displayName: Torque saturation }
  admissible: { displayName: Passes the gates }
  refused_for: { displayName: Refused for }
  feedforward: { displayName: Feed-forward }
style:
  chrome: minimal
  numbers: { digits: 3, compact: true }
  # WHY one fixed colour per rung, the same in every panel (tiles, time series, paths, the nine robots' charts): Zach's
  # "all of those things synced" reads only if tuned is the same blue everywhere; the target is the muted dashed ink
  palette: { target: "#8b9099", factory: "#e8743b", analytic: "#9b6ad6", tuned: "#2a78d6", oracle: "#19a979" }
rerun:
  rrd: rerun/pid-tuning.rrd
  sdk: 0.40.0
clock:
  data: samples
  time: t
  fps: 30
datasets:
  samples:
    data: samples.json
    label: UR5e replay
    facets:
      - { property: joint, as: select, label: Joint }
    # the elbow to start: the tuned rung's worst joint on tracking RMS and stop p90 (kpis.json tracking_rms_joint)
    filters: 'joint == "elbow_joint"'
  lever: step.json
  tool: tool.json
  robot: robot.json
  media: media.json
  kpis: kpis.json
  headline: headline.json
  joints: joints.json
  gains: gains.json
  robots: robots.json
  fidelity:
    data: fidelity.json
    label: The rack (real)
    facets: [servo, ff_fraction]
links:
  - { from: gains.robot_id, to: robots.robot_id }
layout:
  panels:
    - text: |
        ## UR5e: factory gains to tuned, in simulation
        pidtuna tunes the UR5e's six joints four ways: the **factory** gains, the **analytic** first guess, the
        **tuned** result and the **oracle** (the best any gains can do against the hidden true plant), then replays one
        coordinated tape with each. **Everything in this top half is simulation**: pidtuna's ArmSim against a plant with
        illustrative parameters, and the videos are **MuJoCo renders (sim), not a camera**. **No real UR5e run
        exists**, so there is no measured trace or camera clip to set beside them. The tiles are the worst of the six
        joints; errors are mrad. Pick a joint in the rail, then press play or scrub: the videos, both time series, the
        tool path and the 3D arm follow one clock. The export has no overshoot or settling time.
      w: 12
    # WHY title: none on the KPI tiles: the card's own label is the tile's title (Klipfolio's tiles), not a second one
    - { view: Stop p90 · tuned, w: 3, style: { title: none } }
    - { view: Tracking RMS · tuned, w: 3, style: { title: none } }
    - { view: × better than factory, w: 3, style: { title: none } }
    - { view: Tracking RMS by rung, w: 3 }
    - { view: Playback, w: 12 }
    - { view: Joint angle vs target, w: 8, h: 3 }
    - { view: MuJoCo replay · tuned (sim), w: 4, h: 3 }
    - { view: Error over time, w: 8, h: 3 }
    - { view: Factory vs tuned (sim), w: 4, h: 3 }
    - { view: Tool path 3D (sim FK), w: 6, h: 4 }
    - { view: Tool path XZ (sim FK), w: 6, h: 4 }
    - { view: Lever · pick-and-place (sim), w: 12, h: 3 }
    - { view: Gates per joint · factory → oracle, w: 6 }
    - { view: Torque saturation by rung, w: 6 }
    - { view: UR5e gain vs error, w: 4, h: 4 }
    - { view: UR5e gains per joint, w: 8, h: 4 }
    - text: |
        ## All nine robots: how close the tuner gets to the oracle
        Each robot's joints are tuned the same four ways. These are pidtuna's **simulated** robots with illustrative
        parameters (hollow marks: estimates), so read the ladder, not the absolute numbers. Errors are mrad for joints
        and mm for the belt axes (conveyor, gantry). The data has no overshoot or settling time: pidtuna scores *stop
        p90*, *tracking RMS*, *max error* and *ringing*.
      w: 12
    - { view: Tuned against the oracle, w: 12, h: 3 }
    - { view: Gain vs error, w: 7, h: 5 }
    - { view: Error by rung, w: 5, h: 5 }
    - { views: [Every joint, Robot × rung], title: Per joint and motor, w: 12, h: 5 }
    - text: |
        ### Does the sim plant match the real rack?
        The one **real** comparison: the tuner's sim plant against the rack's servos (CAN 4, 11-14), stop p90 with and
        without Coulomb feed-forward. Points on the diagonal agree; this dataset has no link to the robots above, so
        their rail leaves it alone.
      w: 12
    - { view: Sim vs real stop p90, w: 6, h: 4 }
    - { view: Fidelity by servo, w: 6, h: 4 }
views:
  # ---- the UR5e's tiles (headline.json, kpis.json: the producer's worst-joint scores, sim)
  - type: kpi
    name: Stop p90 · tuned
    from: headline
    filters: 'situation == "tuned"'
    kpi:
      label: Stop p90 · tuned (worst joint)
      value: { property: stop_p90 }
      compare: { against: factory_stop_p90, better: lower }
  - type: kpi
    name: Tracking RMS · tuned
    from: headline
    filters: 'situation == "tuned"'
    kpi:
      label: Tracking RMS · tuned (worst joint)
      value: { property: tracking_rms }
      compare: { against: oracle_tracking_rms, better: lower }
  - type: kpi
    name: × better than factory
    from: kpis
    filters: 'situation == "tuned"'
    kpi:
      label: × better than factory · tuned
      value: { property: vs_factory }
  - type: barlist
    name: Tracking RMS by rung
    from: kpis
    barlist: { label: situation, value: { property: tracking_rms }, better: lower }
  # ---- the clock
  - type: playback
    name: Playback
    playback: { speeds: [0.25, 0.5, 1, 2], range: true, readout: true }
  # ---- the rail's joint, sample by sample (samples.json, sim)
  - type: timeseries
    name: Joint angle vs target
    from: samples
    timeseries:
      x: t
      y: q_deg
      series: situation
      unit: °
      dash: [target]
      legend: top
  # WHY symlog: factory's error is ~100 mrad and the tuned and oracle rungs' under 1 mrad; a linear axis flattens the
  # rungs the tuner is about into the zero line
  - type: timeseries
    name: Error over time
    from: samples
    filters: 'situation != "target"'
    timeseries:
      x: t
      y: err_mrad
      series: situation
      unit: mrad
      scale: symlog
      legend: top
      # the tuned rung's worst-joint tracking RMS, kpis.json tracking_rms (tuned, elbow_joint) = 0.4333 mrad; the
      # export has no numeric gate to draw
      rules: [{ y: 0.4333, label: "tuned RMS 0.433 (worst joint)" }, { y: -0.4333 }]
  # ---- the MuJoCo renders (media.json: sim-render, t0 0)
  - type: video
    name: MuJoCo replay · tuned (sim)
    from: media
    filters: 'situation == "tuned"'
    video: { src: src, label: situation, primary: true }
  - type: video-compare
    name: Factory vs tuned (sim)
    from: media
    overlay: { by: situation, a: factory, b: tuned, mode: wipe, split: 0.5 }
  # ---- the tool (tool.json: MuJoCo forward kinematics of the replayed joint angles, sim)
  # the 3D card reads robot.json (source/build_robot.py): the same FK as each link's pose at 25 Hz, so Menagerie's UR5e
  # meshes (media/ur5e_links.glb) stand where the arm was; the stick (the link origins, then the tool) is the fallback
  - type: scene3d
    name: Tool path 3D (sim FK)
    from: robot
    scene3d:
      x: px
      y: py
      z: pz
      series: situation
      target: target
      t: t
      skeleton: [[base_x, base_y, base_z], [shoulder_link_x, shoulder_link_y, shoulder_link_z], [upper_arm_link_x, upper_arm_link_y, upper_arm_link_z], [forearm_link_x, forearm_link_y, forearm_link_z], [wrist_1_link_x, wrist_1_link_y, wrist_1_link_z], [wrist_2_link_x, wrist_2_link_y, wrist_2_link_z], [wrist_3_link_x, wrist_3_link_y, wrist_3_link_z], [px, py, pz]]
      robot:
        model: media/ur5e_links.glb
        links: [base, shoulder_link, upper_arm_link, forearm_link, wrist_1_link, wrist_2_link, wrist_3_link]
        ghost: target
  - type: trajectory
    name: Tool path XZ (sim FK)
    from: tool
    trajectory: { x: px, y: pz, series: situation, target: target, t: t, trail: true }
  # ---- the lever (step.json: 1 joint, pickplace tape, 100 Hz, sim; 8.67 s, longer than the UR5e's 7.9 s clock)
  - type: timeseries
    name: Lever · pick-and-place (sim)
    from: lever
    timeseries:
      x: t
      y: q_deg
      series: situation
      unit: °
      dash: [target]
      legend: top
  # ---- the ladder per joint (joints.json, kpis.json)
  - type: tracker
    name: Gates per joint · factory → oracle
    from: joints
    groupBy: { property: joint }
    sort:
      - { property: order, direction: ASC }
    tracker: { state: admissible, label: situation, tones: { "true": good, "false": bad } }
  - type: bullet
    name: Torque saturation by rung
    from: kpis
    sort:
      - { property: order, direction: ASC }
    bullet: { value: { property: saturation }, label: title, better: lower }
  - type: chart
    name: UR5e gain vs error
    from: joints
    chart:
      mark: { type: point, filled: true, size: 70 }
      encoding:
        x: { field: kp, scale: { type: log }, title: Kp }
        y: { field: tracking_rms_mrad, scale: { type: log }, title: Tracking RMS (mrad) }
        color: { field: situation, title: Rung, sort: [factory, analytic, tuned, oracle] }
    hover: { title: joint, fields: [situation, kp, kd, tracking_rms_mrad, stop_p90_mrad] }
  - type: table
    name: UR5e gains per joint
    from: joints
    order: [joint, situation, kp, kd, feedforward, tracking_rms_mrad, stop_p90_mrad, max_error_mrad, ringing_mrad, saturation, admissible, refused_for]
    # WHY plain text: joints.json's badge slots colour the rungs unlike style.palette (factory would be green here)
    display: { situation: text }
    sort:
      - { property: joint, direction: ASC }
      - { property: order, direction: ASC }
  # ---- all nine robots (round 1: gains.json, robots.json, fidelity.json)
  - type: kpi
    name: Tuned against the oracle
    from: robots
    select: robot_id
    groupBy: { property: robot }
    kpi:
      value: { property: tuned_tracking_rms }
      compare: { against: oracle_tracking_rms, better: lower, neutral: 0.05 }
  - type: chart
    name: Gain vs error
    from: gains
    select: robot_id
    chart:
      mark: { type: point, size: 70 }
      encoding:
        x: { field: kp, scale: { type: log }, title: Kp }
        y: { field: tracking_rms, scale: { type: log }, title: Tracking RMS (mrad; mm for belt axes) }
        color: { field: rung, title: Rung, sort: [factory, analytic, tuned, oracle] }
        shape: { field: robot, title: Robot }
    hover: { title: joint, fields: [robot, rung, kp, kd, tracking_rms, stop_p90, feedforward] }
  - type: chart
    name: Error by rung
    from: gains
    select: rung
    chart:
      mark: bar
      encoding:
        x: { field: rung, sort: [factory, analytic, tuned, oracle], title: null }
        y: { field: tracking_rms, aggregate: median, scale: { type: log }, title: Median tracking RMS }
        color: { field: rung, sort: [factory, analytic, tuned, oracle], legend: null }
  - type: table
    name: Every joint
    from: gains
    order: [robot, joint, rung, kp, kd, feedforward, tracking_rms, stop_p90, max_error, ringing, improvement]
    # WHY plain text: gains.json's badge slots colour the rungs unlike style.palette (factory would be green here)
    display: { rung: text }
    sort:
      - { property: robot_id, direction: ASC }
      - { property: joint, direction: ASC }
      - { property: rung_order, direction: ASC }
  - type: pivot
    name: Robot × rung
    from: gains
    groupBy: { property: robot }
    splitBy: [rung]
    value: { property: tracking_rms, summary: Median }
  - type: chart
    name: Sim vs real stop p90
    from: fidelity
    chart:
      mark: { type: point, filled: true, size: 90 }
      encoding:
        x: { field: real_p90, title: Real stop p90 (mrad) }
        y: { field: sim_p90, title: Sim stop p90 (mrad) }
        color: { field: servo, title: Servo }
        shape: { field: ff_fraction, type: nominal, title: Coulomb ff }
    guides:
      - { indexLine: { slope: 1, through: 1 }, label: "sim = real" }
    hover: { title: servo, fields: [ff_fraction, real_p90, sim_p90, real_tracking_rms, sim_tracking_rms, gap_p90] }
  - type: table
    name: Fidelity by servo
    from: fidelity
    order: [servo, ff_fraction, real_p90, sim_p90, gap_p90, real_tracking_rms, sim_tracking_rms, real_coulomb_nm, truth_coulomb_nm]
    sort:
      - { property: can_id, direction: ASC }
